12, and 32 were reported.\nEASI-75 response was defined as at least 75% improvement from baseline in EASI total score.\nThe EASI score was used to measure the severity and extent of AD and measures erythema, infiltration&#x2F;papulation, excoriation and lichenification on 4 anatomic regions of the body: head&#x2F;neck, trunk, upper and lower extremities.\nThe severity of the clinical signs of AD for each of 4 body regions was scored on a 4-point scale: 0=absent, 1=mild, 2=moderate and 3=severe.\nThe total EASI score is the sum of four body-region scores ranged from 0 (minimum) to 72 (maximum) points, with the higher scores reflecting the worse severity of AD.","populationDescription":"FAS included all randomized participants who received at least 1 dose of study agent.\nHere, n (number analyzed) signifies number of participants who were analyzed at the specified timepoints and &#x27;0&#x27; in the number analyzed field signifies that none of the participants were evaluable at the specified timepoint.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"NUMBER","unitOfMeasure":"percentage of participants","timeFrame":"Weeks 4, 8, 12, and 32","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Placebo (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received placebo matching to bermekimab (4 milliliters [mL]) subcutaneous (SC) injection at Week 0, followed by weekly (qw) placebo SC injections from Week 1 through Week 16."},{"id":"OG001","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg q2w (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received bermekimab 800 milligrams (mg) (400mg*2) loading dose SC injection at Week 0 followed by bermekimab 400 mg SC injections every 2 weeks (q2w) alternating with matching placebo q2w through Week 16."},{"id":"OG002","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received bermekimab 400 mg loading dose SC injection along with matching placebo loading dose SC injection at Week 0 followed by weekly (qw) SC injections of bermekimab 400 mg (2*200 mg per mL) through Week 16."},{"id":"OG003","title":"Placebo Then Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants were crossed-over to active treatment period and received bermekimab 400 mg SC injection qw at Week 16 through Week 31."},{"id":"OG004","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg q2w (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants entered active treatment period and continued to receive bermekimab 400 mg SC injection q2w alternating with matching placebo through Week 31."},{"id":"OG005","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants entered active treatment period and continued to receive bermekimab 400 mg SC injection qw through Week 31."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"28"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"27"}]}],"classes":[{"title":"Week 4","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"0"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"10.3"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"17.2"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"10.3"}]}]},{"title":"Week 8","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"0"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"10.3"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"13.8"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"17.2"}]}]},{"title":"Week 12","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"0"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"13.8"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"20.7"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"37.9"}]}]},{"title":"Week 32","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"28"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"27"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG003","value":"77.8"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"69.0"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"65.5"}]}]}]},{"type":"SECONDARY","title":"Percentage of Participants With an Investigators Global Assessment (IGA) Score of 0 or 1 and a Reduction From Baseline of &gt;=2 Points at Week 16","description":"Percentage of participants with both IGA score of 0 or 1 and a reduction from baseline of &gt;=2 points was reported.\nIGA assesses AD severity and clinical response using a 5-point scale: 0 = clear, 1= almost clear, 2 = mild, 3 = moderate, 4 = severe.\nA higher score indicated more severity of AD.\nThe score was determined by ranking the extent of erythema and population&#x2F;infiltration.\nA clinical response to therapy was an IGA score of 0 (clear) or 1 (almost clear).\nThis outcome measure was planned to be analyzed for specified arms only.","populationDescription":"FAS included all randomized participants who received at least 1 dose of study agent.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"NUMBER","unitOfMeasure":"percentage of participants","timeFrame":"Week 16","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Placebo (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received placebo matching to bermekimab (4 milliliters [mL]) subcutaneous (SC) injection at Week 0, followed by weekly (qw) placebo SC injections from Week 1 through Week 16."},{"id":"OG001","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg q2w (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received bermekimab 800 milligrams (mg) (400mg*2) loading dose SC injection at Week 0 followed by bermekimab 400 mg SC injections every 2 weeks (q2w) alternating with matching placebo q2w through Week 16."},{"id":"OG002","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received bermekimab 400 mg loading dose SC injection along with matching placebo loading dose SC injection at Week 0 followed by weekly (qw) SC injections of bermekimab 400 mg (2*200 mg per mL) through Week 16."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"}]}],"classes":[{"title":"IGA score of clear (0)","categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"6.9"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"6.9"}]}]},{"title":"IGA score of clear (0) or almost clear (1)","categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"6.9"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"17.2"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"13.8"}]}]},{"title":"IGA score of mild or better (reduction from baseline of &gt;=2 points)","categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"24.1"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"34.5"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"34.5"}]}]}]},{"type":"SECONDARY","title":"Percentage of Participants Achieving EASI-90 Response at Weeks 12, 16, and 32","description":"Percentage of participants achieving EASI-90 response at Weeks 12, 16 and 32 were reported.\nEASI-90 response was defined as at least 90% improvement from baseline in EASI total score.\nThe EASI score was used to measure the severity and extent of atopic dermatitis (AD) and measures erythema, infiltration&#x2F;papulation, excoriation and lichenification on 4 anatomic regions of the body: head&#x2F;neck, trunk, upper and lower extremities.\nThe severity of the clinical signs of AD for each of 4 body regions was scored on a 4-point scale: 0=absent, 1=mild, 2=moderate and 3=severe.\nThe total EASI score is the sum of four body-region scores ranged from 0 (minimum) to 72 (maximum) points, with the higher scores reflecting the worse severity of AD.","populationDescription":"FAS; N (number of participants analyzed)=participants evaluated for this outcome measure, n (number analyzed)=participants analyzed at specified timepoints, 0=no participant analyzed.\nWeek 16 data were collected and analyzed only for placebo crossover participants during active treatment period as pre-planned.\nFor active treatment period assessments, participants who discontinued placebo controlled period in Bermekimab 400 mg q2w and Bermekimab 400 mg qw arms were also included as pre-planned.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"NUMBER","unitOfMeasure":"percentage of participants","timeFrame":"Weeks 12, 16, and 32","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Placebo (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received placebo matching to bermekimab (4 milliliters [mL]) subcutaneous (SC) injection at Week 0, followed by weekly (qw) placebo SC injections from Week 1 through Week 16."},{"id":"OG001","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg q2w (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received bermekimab 800 milligrams (mg) (400mg*2) loading dose SC injection at Week 0 followed by bermekimab 400 mg SC injections every 2 weeks (q2w) alternating with matching placebo q2w through Week 16."},{"id":"OG002","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received bermekimab 400 mg loading dose SC injection along with matching placebo loading dose SC injection at Week 0 followed by weekly (qw) SC injections of bermekimab 400 mg (2*200 mg per mL) through Week 16."},{"id":"OG003","title":"Placebo Then Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants were crossed-over to active treatment period and received bermekimab 400 mg SC injection qw at Week 16 through Week 31."},{"id":"OG004","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg q2w (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants entered active treatment period and continued to receive bermekimab 400 mg SC injection q2w alternating with matching placebo through Week 31."},{"id":"OG005","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants entered active treatment period and continued to receive bermekimab 400 mg SC injection qw through Week 31."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"29"}]}],"classes":[{"title":"Week 12","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"0"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"6.9"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"6.9"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"10.3"}]}]},{"title":"Week 16","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"0"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"10.3"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"10.3"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"0"}]}]},{"title":"Week 32","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"29"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG003","value":"37.0"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"24.1"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"34.5"}]}]}]},{"type":"SECONDARY","title":"Change From Baseline in Dermatology Life Quality Index (DLQI) at Weeks 8, 12, 16, and 32","description":"The DLQI is a 10-item, validated questionnaire used in clinical practice and clinical trials to assess the impact of AD disease symptoms and treatment on quality of life (QOL).\nThe format is a simple response (0 to 3 where 0 is &quot;not at all&quot; and 3 is &quot;very much&quot;) to 10 questions, which assess QOL over the past week, with an overall scoring system of 0 to 30.\nThe DLQI is calculated by summing the score of each question resulting in a maximum of 30 and a minimum of 0. A higher score indicates more severe disease and poor QoL.","populationDescription":"FAS; N (number of participants analyzed)=participants evaluated for this outcome measure, n (number analyzed)=participants analyzed at specified timepoints, 0=no participant analyzed.\nWeek 16 data were collected and analyzed only for placebo crossover participants during active treatment period as pre-planned.\nFor active treatment period assessments, participants who discontinued placebo controlled period in Bermekimab 400 mg q2w and Bermekimab 400 mg qw arms were also included as pre-planned.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"MEAN","dispersionType":"Standard Deviation","unitOfMeasure":"score on a scale","timeFrame":"Baseline, Weeks 8, 12, 16 and 32","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Placebo (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received placebo matching to bermekimab (4 milliliters [mL]) subcutaneous (SC) injection at Week 0, followed by weekly (qw) placebo SC injections from Week 1 through Week 16."},{"id":"OG001","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg q2w (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received bermekimab 800 milligrams (mg) (400mg*2) loading dose SC injection at Week 0 followed by bermekimab 400 mg SC injections every 2 weeks (q2w) alternating with matching placebo q2w through Week 16."},{"id":"OG002","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received bermekimab 400 mg loading dose SC injection along with matching placebo loading dose SC injection at Week 0 followed by weekly (qw) SC injections of bermekimab 400 mg (2*200 mg per mL) through Week 16."},{"id":"OG003","title":"Placebo Then Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants were crossed-over to active treatment period and received bermekimab 400 mg SC injection qw at Week 16 through Week 31."},{"id":"OG004","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg q2w (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants entered active treatment period and continued to receive bermekimab 400 mg SC injection q2w alternating with matching placebo through Week 31."},{"id":"OG005","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants entered active treatment period and continued to receive bermekimab 400 mg SC injection qw through Week 31."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"29"}]}],"classes":[{"title":"Week 8","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"0"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"-4.86","spread":"5.598"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"-3.03","spread":"4.136"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"-3.41","spread":"4.694"}]}]},{"title":"Week 12","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"28"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"0"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"-4.86","spread":"5.774"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"-3.29","spread":"3.505"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"-4.72","spread":"5.028"}]}]},{"title":"Week 16","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"0"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"-6.07","spread":"7.151"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"-3.38","spread":"3.886"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"-5.93","spread":"5.120"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"-6.52","spread":"7.213"}]}]},{"title":"Week 32","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"29"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG003","value":"-9.15","spread":"6.413"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"-4.10","spread":"5.759"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"-7.76","spread":"6.122"}]}]}]},{"type":"SECONDARY","title":"Change From Baseline in Hospital Anxiety and Depression Scale (HADS) (Anxiety) Score at Weeks 8, 12, 16, and 32","description":"In this outcome measure, change from baseline in HADS-Anxiety score at weeks 8, 12, 16 and 32 were reported.\nThe HADS is an instrument for screening anxiety and depression in non-psychiatric populations; repeated administration also provides information about changes to a participant&#x27;s emotional state.\nThe HADS is a 14-item self-administered questionnaire, 7 each for anxiety and depression symptoms.\nEach item is scored from 0-3, resulting in total anxiety score ranging from 0 (less severity of anxiety) to 21 (greater severity of anxiety).\nHigher score indicated more anxiety symptoms.\nThe following cut-off scores are recommended: 7 to 8 for possible presence, 10 to 11 for probable presence, and 14 to 15 for severe anxiety.","populationDescription":"FAS; N (number of participants analyzed)=participants evaluated for this outcome measure, n (number analyzed)=participants analyzed at specified timepoints, 0=no participant analyzed.\nWeek 16 data were collected and analyzed only for placebo crossover participants during active treatment period as pre-planned.\nFor active treatment period assessments, participants who discontinued placebo controlled period in Bermekimab 400 mg q2w and Bermekimab 400 mg qw arms were also included as pre-planned.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"MEAN","dispersionType":"Standard Deviation","unitOfMeasure":"score on a scale","timeFrame":"Baseline, Weeks 8,12,16 and 32","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Placebo (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received placebo matching to bermekimab (4 milliliters [mL]) subcutaneous (SC) injection at Week 0, followed by weekly (qw) placebo SC injections from Week 1 through Week 16."},{"id":"OG001","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg q2w (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received bermekimab 800 milligrams (mg) (400mg*2) loading dose SC injection at Week 0 followed by bermekimab 400 mg SC injections every 2 weeks (q2w) alternating with matching placebo q2w through Week 16."},{"id":"OG002","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received bermekimab 400 mg loading dose SC injection along with matching placebo loading dose SC injection at Week 0 followed by weekly (qw) SC injections of bermekimab 400 mg (2*200 mg per mL) through Week 16."},{"id":"OG003","title":"Placebo Then Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants were crossed-over to active treatment period and received bermekimab 400 mg SC injection qw at Week 16 through Week 31."},{"id":"OG004","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg q2w (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants entered active treatment period and continued to receive bermekimab 400 mg SC injection q2w alternating with matching placebo through Week 31."},{"id":"OG005","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants entered active treatment period and continued to receive bermekimab 400 mg SC injection qw through Week 31."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"29"}]}],"classes":[{"title":"Week 8","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"0"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"1.59","spread":"2.732"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"2.00","spread":"3.770"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"1.90","spread":"2.257"}]}]},{"title":"Week 12","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"28"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"0"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"1.45","spread":"2.898"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"1.89","spread":"3.755"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"2.62","spread":"2.846"}]}]},{"title":"Week 16","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"0"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"1.59","spread":"2.771"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"1.97","spread":"3.669"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"2.66","spread":"3.062"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"1.70","spread":"2.839"}]}]},{"title":"Week 32","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"29"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG003","value":"2.93","spread":"3.419"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"2.34","spread":"3.467"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"3.14","spread":"3.114"}]}]}]},{"type":"SECONDARY","title":"Change From Baseline in HADS (Depression) Score at Weeks 8, 12, 16, and 32","description":"In this outcome measure, change from baseline in HADS-depression score at weeks 8, 12, 16 and 32 were reported.\nThe HADS is an instrument for screening anxiety and depression in non-psychiatric populations; repeated administration also provides information about changes to a participant&#x27;s emotional state.\nThe HADS is a 14-item self-administered questionnaire, and consists of 7 items each for anxiety and depression symptoms.\nEach item is scored from 0-3, resulting in total depression score ranging from 0 (less severity of depression) to 21 (greater severity of depression).\nHigher score indicated more depression symptoms.\nThe following cut-off scores are recommended: 7 to 8 for possible presence, 10 to 11 for probable presence, and 14 to 15 for severe depression.","populationDescription":"FAS; N (number of participants analyzed)=participants evaluated for this outcome measure, n (number analyzed)=participants analyzed at specified timepoints, 0=no participant analyzed.\nWeek 16 data were collected and analyzed only for placebo crossover participants during active treatment period as pre-planned.\nFor active treatment period assessments, participants who discontinued placebo controlled period in Bermekimab 400 mg q2w and Bermekimab 400 mg qw arms were also included as pre-planned.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"MEAN","dispersionType":"Standard Deviation","unitOfMeasure":"score on a scale","timeFrame":"Baseline, Weeks 8,12,16 and 32","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Placebo (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received placebo matching to bermekimab (4 milliliters [mL]) subcutaneous (SC) injection at Week 0, followed by weekly (qw) placebo SC injections from Week 1 through Week 16."},{"id":"OG001","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg q2w (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received bermekimab 800 milligrams (mg) (400mg*2) loading dose SC injection at Week 0 followed by bermekimab 400 mg SC injections every 2 weeks (q2w) alternating with matching placebo q2w through Week 16."},{"id":"OG002","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received bermekimab 400 mg loading dose SC injection along with matching placebo loading dose SC injection at Week 0 followed by weekly (qw) SC injections of bermekimab 400 mg (2*200 mg per mL) through Week 16."},{"id":"OG003","title":"Placebo Then Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants were crossed-over to active treatment period and received bermekimab 400 mg SC injection qw at Week 16 through Week 31."},{"id":"OG004","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg q2w (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants entered active treatment period and continued to receive bermekimab 400 mg SC injection q2w alternating with matching placebo through Week 31."},{"id":"OG005","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants entered active treatment period and continued to receive bermekimab 400 mg SC injection qw through Week 31."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"29"}]}],"classes":[{"title":"Week 8","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"0"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"0.86","spread":"1.941"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"0.59","spread":"3.088"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"1.31","spread":"2.904"}]}]},{"title":"Week 12","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"28"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"0"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"0.97","spread":"2.291"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"0.57","spread":"3.132"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"0.90","spread":"3.426"}]}]},{"title":"Week 16","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"0"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"0.93","spread":"2.103"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"0.31","spread":"2.989"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"1.07","spread":"3.139"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"1.00","spread":"2.166"}]}]},{"title":"Week 32","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"29"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG003","value":"1.93","spread":"2.235"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"0.28","spread":"3.401"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"1.55","spread":"4.188"}]}]}]},{"type":"SECONDARY","title":"Change From Baseline in Patient Oriented Eczema Measure (POEM) Scores at Weeks 8, 12, 16, and 32","description":"The POEM is a 7-item, validated questionnaire used to assess disease symptoms in both children and adults.\nParticipants respond to 7 questions, including dryness, itching, flaking, cracking, sleep loss, bleeding, and weeping, each scored on a 5-point scale based on frequency of occurrence during the previous week: 0 = no days, 1 = 1 to 2 days, 2 = 3 to 4 days, 3 = 5 to 6 days, and 4 = all days.\nItem scores are added to provide a total score ranging from 0 (clear) to 28 (very severe atopic eczema).\nHigher scores indicated more severe disease and poor quality of life.","populationDescription":"FAS; N (number of participants analyzed)=participants evaluated for this outcome measure, n (number analyzed)=participants analyzed at specified timepoints, 0=no participant analyzed.\nWeek 16 data were collected and analyzed only for placebo crossover participants during active treatment period as pre-planned.\nFor active treatment period assessments, participants who discontinued placebo controlled period in Bermekimab 400 mg q2w and Bermekimab 400 mg qw arms were also included as pre-planned.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"MEAN","dispersionType":"Standard Deviation","unitOfMeasure":"score on a scale","timeFrame":"Baseline, Weeks 8, 12, 16, and 32","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Placebo (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received placebo matching to bermekimab (4 milliliters [mL]) subcutaneous (SC) injection at Week 0, followed by weekly (qw) placebo SC injections from Week 1 through Week 16."},{"id":"OG001","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg q2w (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received bermekimab 800 milligrams (mg) (400mg*2) loading dose SC injection at Week 0 followed by bermekimab 400 mg SC injections every 2 weeks (q2w) alternating with matching placebo q2w through Week 16."},{"id":"OG002","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received bermekimab 400 mg loading dose SC injection along with matching placebo loading dose SC injection at Week 0 followed by weekly (qw) SC injections of bermekimab 400 mg (2*200 mg per mL) through Week 16."},{"id":"OG003","title":"Placebo Then Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants were crossed-over to active treatment period and received bermekimab 400 mg SC injection qw at Week 16 through Week 31."},{"id":"OG004","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg q2w (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants entered active treatment period and continued to receive bermekimab 400 mg SC injection q2w alternating with matching placebo through Week 31."},{"id":"OG005","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants entered active treatment period and continued to receive bermekimab 400 mg SC injection qw through Week 31."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"29"}]}],"classes":[{"title":"Week 8","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"0"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"-4.79","spread":"3.949"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"-5.66","spread":"5.627"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"-6.59","spread":"4.939"}]}]},{"title":"Week 12","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"28"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"0"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"-5.07","spread":"5.021"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"-6.14","spread":"5.543"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"-7.55","spread":"4.903"}]}]},{"title":"Week 16","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"0"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"-5.76","spread":"5.680"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"-6.00","spread":"5.542"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"-8.07","spread":"5.618"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"-6.19","spread":"5.657"}]}]},{"title":"Week 32","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"29"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG003","value":"-10.48","spread":"6.659"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"-8.66","spread":"6.726"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"-10.66","spread":"6.800"}]}]}]},{"type":"SECONDARY","title":"Change From Baseline in SCORing Atopic Dermatitis (SCORAD) Total Score at Weeks 8, 12, 16, and 32.","description":"SCORAD is a validated scoring index for AD, which consists of 3 components that is A =extent or affected body surface area assessed as percentage of each defined body area and reported as the sum of all areas, with a maximum score of 100%.\nB=severity of 6 specific symptoms of AD (redness, swelling, oozing&#x2F;crusting, excoriation, skin thickening&#x2F;lichenification, dryness) assessed using the following scale: none (0), mild (1), moderate (2), or severe (3) (for a maximum of 18 total points) and C=subjective symptoms scored by participants on visual analogue scale, where &quot;0&quot; is no itch (or no sleeplessness) and &quot;10&quot; is worst imaginable itch (or sleeplessness) with a maximum score of 20.\nSCORAD total score was calculated using these 3 aspects: extent (A: 0-100), severity (B: 0-18), and subjective symptoms (C: 0-20) using the formula: A&#x2F;5 + 7*B&#x2F;2+ C to give the SCORAD total score range of 0 to 103, where 0 = no disease to 103 = severe disease.\nHigher values of SCORAD represent worse outcome.","populationDescription":"FAS; N (number of participants analyzed)=participants evaluated for this outcome measure, n (number analyzed)=participants analyzed at specified timepoints, 0=no participant analyzed.\nWeek 16 data were collected and analyzed only for placebo crossover participants during active treatment period as pre-planned.\nFor active treatment period assessments, participants who discontinued placebo controlled period in Bermekimab 400 mg q2w and Bermekimab 400 mg qw arms were also included as pre-planned.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"MEAN","dispersionType":"Standard Deviation","unitOfMeasure":"score on a scale","timeFrame":"Baseline to Weeks 8, 12, 16 and 32","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Placebo (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received placebo matching to bermekimab (4 milliliters [mL]) subcutaneous (SC) injection at Week 0, followed by weekly (qw) placebo SC injections from Week 1 through Week 16."},{"id":"OG001","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg q2w (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received bermekimab 800 milligrams (mg) (400mg*2) loading dose SC injection at Week 0 followed by bermekimab 400 mg SC injections every 2 weeks (q2w) alternating with matching placebo q2w through Week 16."},{"id":"OG002","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received bermekimab 400 mg loading dose SC injection along with matching placebo loading dose SC injection at Week 0 followed by weekly (qw) SC injections of bermekimab 400 mg (2*200 mg per mL) through Week 16."},{"id":"OG003","title":"Placebo Then Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants were crossed-over to active treatment period and received bermekimab 400 mg SC injection qw at Week 16 through Week 31."},{"id":"OG004","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg q2w (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants entered active treatment period and continued to receive bermekimab 400 mg SC injection q2w alternating with matching placebo through Week 31."},{"id":"OG005","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants entered active treatment period and continued to receive bermekimab 400 mg SC injection qw through Week 31."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"29"}]}],"classes":[{"title":"Week 8","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"0"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"21.53","spread":"11.468"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"21.29","spread":"15.632"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"19.39","spread":"11.632"}]}]},{"title":"Week 12","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"28"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"0"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"24.27","spread":"13.130"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"26.50","spread":"12.894"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"22.45","spread":"12.849"}]}]},{"title":"Week 16","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"0"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"25.90","spread":"15.916"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"27.56","spread":"13.661"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"24.11","spread":"14.961"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27.82","spread":"14.743"}]}]},{"title":"Week 32","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"0"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"29"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG003","value":"44.35","spread":"16.479"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"31.92","spread":"18.467"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"35.05","spread":"18.461"}]}]}]},{"type":"SECONDARY","title":"Change From Baseline in Global Individual Signs Score (GISS) at Weeks 8, 12, 16, and 32.","description":"GISS assesses AD lesions for erythema, excoriations, lichenification and edema&#x2F;papulation.\nEach component was rated on a global basis (over the entire body surface rather than region) using a 4-point scale (0=none, 1=mild, 2=moderate and 3=severe) according to the EASI grading severity.\nThe cumulative score, which ranges from 0 to 12, is the sum of the four components.\nA higher score indicates more severe disease.","populationDescription":"FAS; N (number of participants analyzed)=participants evaluated for this outcome measure, n (number analyzed)=participants analyzed at specified timepoints, 0=no participant analyzed.\nWeek 16 data were collected and analyzed only for placebo crossover participants during active treatment period as pre-planned.\nFor active treatment period assessments, participants who discontinued placebo controlled period in Bermekimab 400 mg q2w and Bermekimab 400 mg qw arms were also included as pre-planned.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"MEAN","dispersionType":"Standard Deviation","unitOfMeasure":"score on a scale","timeFrame":"Baseline, Weeks 8,12,16 and 32","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Placebo (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received placebo matching to bermekimab (4 milliliters [mL]) subcutaneous (SC) injection at Week 0, followed by weekly (qw) placebo SC injections from Week 1 through Week 16."},{"id":"OG001","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg q2w (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received bermekimab 800 milligrams (mg) (400mg*2) loading dose SC injection at Week 0 followed by bermekimab 400 mg SC injections every 2 weeks (q2w) alternating with matching placebo q2w through Week 16."},{"id":"OG002","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 0 - 16)","description":"Participants received bermekimab 400 mg loading dose SC injection along with matching placebo loading dose SC injection at Week 0 followed by weekly (qw) SC injections of bermekimab 400 mg (2*200 mg per mL) through Week 16."},{"id":"OG003","title":"Placebo Then Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants were crossed-over to active treatment period and received bermekimab 400 mg SC injection qw at Week 16 through Week 31."},{"id":"OG004","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg q2w (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants entered active treatment period and continued to receive bermekimab 400 mg SC injection q2w alternating with matching placebo through Week 31."},{"id":"OG005","title":"Bermekimab 400 mg qw (Week 16 - 31)","description":"After completion of placebo-controlled period, participants entered active treatment period and continued to receive bermekimab 400 mg SC injection qw through Week 31."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"OG004","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG005","value":"29"}]}],"classes":[{"title":"Week 8","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"29"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"29"},{"gr